      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I have an avatar that has a similar setup which is crashing 100% of the time when activating both Parent particle systems at once. So it definitely looks like it's related to trying to run 1 child particle system with 2 parents. Sucks if this isn't fixable cause it feels more optimized to run just the one child system.\n\nI tested the system in the latest build [1370] and it still seems to be an issue\n\nPulled the particle system into a unity 2022.3.8f1 project to recreate the crash and it also crashes the editor\n\nHere's the part of the Editor.Log around where the crash:\n\n```\n\nAsset Pipeline Refresh (id=8f77bccc3403f4548aa0e6fe4945aee2): Total: 0.003 seconds - Initiated by RefreshV2(AllowForceSynchronousImport)\n\nAssertion failed on expression: 'count >= toIndex'\n\nAssertion failed on expression: 'count >= toIndex'\n\n<RI> Initialized touch support.\n\nAssertion failed on expression: 'particles.array_size() == count'\n\n=================================================================\n\n\tNative Crash Reporting\n\n=================================================================\n\nGot a UNKNOWN while executing native code. This usually indicates\n\na fatal error in the mono runtime or one of the native libraries \n\nused by your application.\n\n=================================================================\n\n=================================================================\n\n\tManaged Stacktrace:\n\n=================================================================\n\n=================================================================\n\nReceived signal SIGSEGV\n\nObtained 31 stack frames\n\n0x00007ff6f6ba309b (Unity) CollisionModule::Update\n\n0x00007ff6f6c0cb39 (Unity) ParticleSystem::UpdateModulesPostSimulationIncremental\n\n0x00007ff6f6c0c0a9 (Unity) ParticleSystem::UpdateModulesIncremental\n\n0x00007ff6f6bfa0d8 (Unity) ParticleSystem::Emit\n\n0x00007ff6f6be3e4e (Unity) RecordEmit\n\n0x00007ff6f6bc29d9 (Unity) SubModule::Update\n\n0x00007ff6f6c0765c (Unity) ParticleSystem::StartModules\n\n0x00007ff6f6c078db (Unity) ParticleSystem::StartParticles\n\n0x00007ff6f6c09249 (Unity) ParticleSystem::Update1Incremental\n\n0x00007ff6f6c09881 (Unity) ParticleSystem::Update1b\n\n0x00007ff6f6c0b545 (Unity) ParticleSystem::UpdateFunction\n\n0x00007ff6f5fbc07c (Unity) ujob_execute_job\n\n0x00007ff6f5fbda90 (Unity) ujob_wait_for\n\n0x00007ff6f5fb8117 (Unity) CompleteFenceInternal\n\n0x00007ff6f6c08701 (Unity) ParticleSystem::SyncJobs\n\n0x00007ff6f6bfb0bb (Unity) ParticleSystem::EndUpdate\n\n0x00007ff6f72456df (Unity) ParticleSystemEffect::UpdateActiveParticleSystemsInternal\n\n0x00007ff6f7245380 (Unity) ParticleSystemEffect::UpdateActiveParticleSystems\n\n0x00007ff6f6bf631b (Unity) ParticleSystem::BeginUpdateAll\n\n0x00007ff6f6bfbc54 (Unity) `ParticleSystem::InitializeClass'::`2'::PreLateUpdateParticleSystemBeginUpdateAllRegistrator::Forward\n\n0x00007ff6f601227a (Unity) ExecutePlayerLoop\n\n0x00007ff6f6012406 (Unity) ExecutePlayerLoop\n\n0x00007ff6f6018cc5 (Unity) PlayerLoop\n\n0x00007ff6f6fdc33f (Unity) PlayerLoopController::InternalUpdateScene\n\n0x00007ff6f6fe8f1d (Unity) PlayerLoopController::UpdateSceneIfNeededFromMainLoop\n\n0x00007ff6f6fe7221 (Unity) Application::TickTimer\n\n0x00007ff6f745d97a (Unity) MainMessageLoop\n\n0x00007ff6f74631e0 (Unity) WinMain\n\n0x00007ff6f884765e (Unity) __scrt_common_main_seh\n\n0x00007ffac30a7344 (KERNEL32) BaseThreadInitThunk\n\n0x00007ffac4fc26b1 (ntdll) RtlUserThreadStart\n\n```",
